Description: core: let stereo3d_unpack be the first filter of a producer
 An editor that takes the views of each 3D clip out side by side, so a project of
 clips with different packings has full side by side frames, needs the filter in
 the clip's producer, not on the consumer. There the producer's rescaling and
 padding filters (swscale, resize) decide the picture's size and shape from the
 frame's width, height, meta.media.width, meta.media.height and aspect_ratio when
 the frame is made, and ask the producer for a picture of the profile's size, so
 the filter got a packed frame already padded to the profile (a half top and
 bottom 1920x1080 frame in a 3840x1080 profile gave 7680x540, the views pillarboxed).
 .
 With in_producer=1, as the first of the producer's filters, the filter tells the
 others in filter_process the size of both views side by side and their shape,
 asks the producer for its own size, and checks it got it. target_views=half is for
 a profile whose frames carry half views squeezed to half their width (1920x1080
 side by side): the shape given is halved, so a pair fills such a frame as the
 profile's own views do; full, or nothing, for whole views. Frame sequences are
 passed on as they are in this place. Without in_producer nothing changes.
 .
 Measured on colour fixtures (left view red, right view blue, a white square),
 profile 3840x1080 and 1920x1080: side by side full and half, top and bottom full
 and half, right eye first; the square comes out square at the full profile and
 half as wide at the half profile, left view on the left.
